  It fits perfectly.  Patience is the key to winning in NetHack.  See
the FAQ if you don't believe me.   A lot of players seem to resent that,
and rightly so.  It means NetHack is a boring game if you play to win.  
(Don't believe me?  Watch some of mrivan's ttyrecs on NAO.)

  That's why so many players pin all their hopes on some instawin item.
People on #nethack obsess over getting a wish, then have no idea what to
wish for.


  Others have pointed out that NetHack doesn't kill you outright as
often as it breaks your will to win.  Nymphs, mindflayers, rust
monsters, disenchanters, BoH explosions, etc. can all cause players to
just give up.  They make suicide seem like a good idea.  Why else is
there a #quit command?  

  If actually playing NetHack solo was good fun then explore mode would
get a lot more use.  Instead it gets almost none.  People seem to play
in wizard mode more than they play in explore mode.  That's because in
wizard mode you can skip all the tedious time and effort necessary to
build up your character.

  (The starting wand of wishing in explore mode?  Don't make me laugh.
Aside from the trouble with luck, alignment(?), and typopos, that's not
